# Vercel serves twin-app/ (the project's Root Directory is "twin-app"), so
# everything below is uploaded for nothing. The API, the Expo app and the local
# tooling are deployed elsewhere -- Railway and EAS -- and none of it is ever
# read by this static site.
backend/
alembic/
alembic.ini
mobile/
tests/
scripts/
docs/
backups/
.tools/
Dockerfile
railway.toml
render.yaml
migrate.py
voice_tunnel.py
*.log

# Superseded page drafts kept for reference, not for serving. auth.js and
# register.html in here still call http://127.0.0.1:8000 directly, which on a
# deployed site points at the visitor's own machine, so publishing them would
# put a dead -- and confusing -- login and signup page on the public origin
# alongside the real ones.
twin-app/.redesign-backup/
